    "semantic_summary": "TrianglePrimitive is a concrete implementation of a geometric primitive, inheriting from MeshData. It encapsulates the necessary vertex data (positions, normals, texture coordinates) and connectivity indices for a standardized 2D triangle. The constructor initializes the geometry with three vertices, defining normals pointing along the Z-axis, and sets up the index buffer [0, 1, 2]. This class serves as a fundamental, self-contained data model for rendering basic triangle shapes within the engine's pipeline."
